### Step 3: the judge option --unit2-family-words (2026-11-09)

The option reads the 18 app specs in docs/storytime/l2-unit2/family-words/, takes the tries from
the cost file of the app folder since U2_FW_RUN.startTime in time order, writes the judge copies
at 360 px to out/storytime-review/judge/prod-u2/, and writes the batch files to
docs/storytime/l2-unit2/judge/prod/. The use of an entry is family-word. The mustShow phrase is
the word, and for the jump word it is "a child jumping with both feet off the ground". The option
refuses --cards, --family-words, and --unit2. The 0-cost failure rule is unchanged: a failed call
still counts as a try, and the script refuses a try with no picture file. The other options of the
script do not change, and the three judge test files pass (28 tests).
The new test file holds 11 tests: 6 spec tests and 5 judge tests.

## Step 4: the app family-word delivery writer (2026-11-09)

`deliverMuseUnit2FamilyWords` in src/storytime/muse-delivery-u2.ts writes the app family-word
delivery. The unit 1 writer `deliverMuseColorSet` refuses these ids, because its row id rule holds
the unit 1 family words only, so the writer lives in the unit 2 file. It takes an approval list of
{ rowId, version (m<n>), colorPrint }, the Muse folder, and the delivery folder. It writes the
color files under the unit 1 family-word name `<id>-v1.png` and one manifest.json in the
StorytimeManifest shape. Each candidate holds the SHA-256 and the pixel size of the print. Every
check runs before the first write: the print is a PNG of 1500 x 1500 pixels, 8-bit, and free of
alpha; an id outside the 18 app family words is refused; an existing delivery folder is refused; a
missing print file stops the write with the id.
The Phase 1 Nit F1 is fixed in the same file: the header comment said 48 reuse rows, and the row
model has 47: 45 rows copy a unit 1 delivery, and 2 rows copy an earlier unit 2 row.
The GREEN command gives 14 files and 232 tests, and the run exits 0. The typecheck
`tsc --noEmit -p .` exits 2: 0 errors in src/storytime, scripts/storytime-*, and tests/storytime-*.
Every error of that run is outside the storytime paths, in assets/*.ts, tests/games/castle-defense,
and tests/part.test.ts.
The new test file holds 17 tests: 6 spec tests, 5 judge tests, and 6 delivery tests.
